{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def is_palindrome(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is a palindrome by comparing its string representation with its reverse.\"\"\"\n    s = str(n)\n    return s == s[::-1]\n\ndef increment_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the next integer after the given number.\"\"\"\n    return n + 1\n\ndef next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the next smallest palindrome greater than the input integer n.\"\"\"\n    current_num = increment_number(n)\n    while not is_palindrome(current_num):\n        current_num = increment_number(current_num)\n    return current_num"}
