{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(input_list: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the item with maximum frequency in a given list.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list (list): List of integers to analyze\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The item that appears most frequently in the list\n    \"\"\"\n    frequencies = {}\n    for item in input_list:\n        frequencies[item] = frequencies.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    max_item = None\n    max_count = -1\n\n    # Iterate through the frequency map to find the item with the highest count.\n    for item, count in frequencies.items():\n        if count > max_count:\n            max_count = count\n            max_item = item\n\n    return max_item"}
