{"task_id": "Mbpp/285", "solution": "def text_match_two_three(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if string contains 'a' followed by exactly 2 or 3 'b' characters.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to check for pattern\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if pattern found, False otherwise\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if input_string[i] == 'a':\n            # Check for at least 'abb'\n            if i + 3 <= n and input_string[i+1:i+3] == 'bb':\n                # Found 'abb'\n                # Check if it extends to 'abbb'\n                if i + 4 <= n and input_string[i+3] == 'b':\n                    # Found 'abbb'\n                    # Now check if it extends to 'abbbb' (which is invalid)\n                    if i + 5 <= n and input_string[i+4] == 'b':\n                        # It's 'abbbb' or longer, so this specific 'a' doesn't match the pattern.\n                        continue # Continue searching from the next character for another potential 'a'.\n                    else:\n                        # It's 'abbb' followed by end of string or non-'b' - this is a valid match.\n                        return True\n                else:\n                    # It's 'abb' followed by end of string or non-'b' - this is a valid match.\n                    return True\n    return False"}
