{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "import itertools\n\ndef _generate_products(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Generates all possible products from elements of two lists.\n    It uses itertools.product for efficient Cartesian product generation.\"\"\"\n    return [x * y for x, y in itertools.product(list1, list2)]\n\ndef _process_results(products, count):\n    \"\"\"Sorts products in descending order and selects the top 'count' elements.\n    The list is sorted in-place before slicing.\"\"\"\n    products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return products[:count]\n\ndef large_product(list1, list2, count):\n    \"\"\"Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists, selecting one factor from each list.\"\"\"\n    all_products = _generate_products(list1, list2)\n    return _process_results(all_products, count)"}
