{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits of each number in a given list.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _extract_digits_sum(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper to sum digits of a single number.\n        It converts the number to a string and sums its individual digit characters.\n        \"\"\"\n        current_sum = 0\n        # Use absolute value to handle potential negative numbers, as sum of digits is typically non-negative.\n        current_number_abs = abs(number)\n        \n        # Convert to string and iterate over characters to sum digits.\n        str_num = str(current_number_abs)\n        for digit_char in str_num:\n            current_sum += int(digit_char)\n        return current_sum\n\n    total_overall_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        total_overall_sum += _extract_digits_sum(number)\n            \n    return total_overall_sum"}
