{"task_id": "Mbpp/427", "solution": "import re\n\ndef change_date_format(date_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a date string from yyyy-mm-dd format to dd-mm-yyyy format.\n    Handles invalid date formats by returning an error message.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate that input dates are in the correct yyyy-mm-dd format.\n    date_pattern = re.compile(r\"^(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})$\")\n    match = date_pattern.match(date_string)\n\n    if not match:\n        # Handle invalid date inputs gracefully by returning a specific error message.\n        return \"Invalid date format\"\n\n    # Extract year, month, and day components from the validated string.\n    year, month, day = match.groups()\n\n    # Convert to dd-mm-yyyy format and return the new string.\n    return f\"{day}-{month}-{year}\""}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(array: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original input array.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a mutable copy of the input array\n    n_array = list(array)\n\n    # Start with a large gap, then reduce it\n    # Using Knuth's gap sequence: h = h * 3 + 1\n    gap = 1\n    while gap < n // 3:\n        gap = gap * 3 + 1\n\n    while gap >= 1:\n        # Perform gapped insertion sort for the current gap size\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            current_value = n_array[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements that are greater than current_value\n            while j >= gap and n_array[j - gap] > current_value:\n                n_array[j] = n_array[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            n_array[j] = current_value\n        \n        # Reduce the gap for the next pass\n        gap //= 3\n        \n    return n_array"}
