{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef combinations_list(input_list: List) -> List[List]:\n    \"\"\"Generate all possible combinations of input list elements.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: List of elements of any type\n\n    Returns:\n        List of lists containing all possible combinations (2^n total)\n    \"\"\"\n    all_combinations = [[]]  # Start with an empty list, representing the empty set\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        # For each element, create new combinations by prepending it\n        # to all existing combinations at the time of processing this element.\n        current_num_combinations = len(all_combinations)\n        for i in range(current_num_combinations):\n            # Create a new combination by taking an existing one and\n            # prepending the current element. This preserves the relative order\n            # of elements that are already in the existing combination.\n            new_combo = [element] + all_combinations[i]\n            all_combinations.append(new_combo)\n            \n    return all_combinations"}
