{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(array: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the maximum product of any contiguous subarray.\n\n    Args:\n        array: List of numeric values\n\n    Returns:\n        Maximum product of contiguous subarray\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0 # Or handle error, but design implies non-empty arrays with array[0] access\n\n    max_ending_here = array[0]\n    min_ending_here = array[0]\n    max_so_far = array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        num = array[i]\n        \n        # Store max_ending_here because it will be updated before min_ending_here needs its old value\n        temp_max = max_ending_here\n\n        max_ending_here = max(num, temp_max * num, min_ending_here * num)\n        min_ending_here = min(num, temp_max * num, min_ending_here * num)\n        \n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
