{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "def last_Digit_Factorial(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given number.\n    Handles special cases for small numbers and the effect of 5 and 0 in factorials.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return 0 # Factorial not defined for negative numbers, though requirement analysis might specify different error handling.\n    elif number < 5:\n        # Calculate factorial directly for small numbers\n        fact = 1\n        for i in range(1, number + 1):\n            fact *= i\n        return fact % 10\n    else:\n        # For number >= 5, the factorial will always end in 0.\n        # This is because 5! = 120, and any factorial greater than 5! will also have factors of 5 and 2,\n        # ensuring a trailing zero.\n        return 0"}
