{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: Tuple[int, int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract all adjacent coordinates in a 3x3 grid centered on the given coordinate.\n    Returns a list of coordinate pairs as [x, y] lists in row-major order.\n    \"\"\"\n    center_x, center_y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            new_x = center_x + dx\n            new_y = center_y + dy\n            adjacent_coords.append([new_x, new_y])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/631", "solution": "def replace_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replace whitespace characters with underscores and vice versa.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to transform\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The transformed string with spaces and underscores swapped\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use a unique temporary character to facilitate bidirectional swapping without conflicts.\n    temp_placeholder = '\\x00'\n\n    # First, replace actual spaces with the temporary placeholder.\n    s_with_temp = input_string.replace(' ', temp_placeholder)\n\n    # Next, replace existing underscores with spaces.\n    s_final_spaces = s_with_temp.replace('_', ' ')\n\n    # Finally, replace the temporary placeholder with underscores.\n    result = s_final_spaces.replace(temp_placeholder, '_')\n\n    return result"}
