{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def _heapify(arr, n, i):\n    # Maintains the max-heap property for the subtree rooted at index i.\n    # It compares the root with its children and swaps if necessary, then recursively heapifies.\n    largest = i\n    left = 2 * i + 1\n    right = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = left\n\n    if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = right\n\n    if largest != i:\n        arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\ndef _build_max_heap(arr):\n    # Transforms an array into a max heap.\n    # It iterates from the last non-leaf node up to the root, applying _heapify.\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\ndef _extract_elements(arr):\n    # Sorts the array in place by repeatedly extracting the maximum element.\n    # It swaps the root with the last element and then heapifies the reduced heap.\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i] # Swap root with current last element\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0) # Heapify the remaining elements\n    return arr\n\ndef heap_sort(input_list):\n    # Sorts a list in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    # It builds a max heap and then extracts elements one by one to sort the list.\n    arr = list(input_list) # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list.\n    \n    _build_max_heap(arr)\n    sorted_arr = _extract_elements(arr)\n    \n    return sorted_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\n\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    Uses the standard metric wind chill formula and rounds the result to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Calculate the wind chill using the standard metric formula.\n    # T_wc = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    # where T is temperature in Celsius and V is wind velocity in km/h.\n    v_power_0_16 = math.pow(wind_velocity, 0.16)\n    \n    wind_chill_raw = (\n        13.12\n        + (0.6215 * temperature)\n        - (11.37 * v_power_0_16)\n        + (0.3965 * temperature * v_power_0_16)\n    )\n    \n    # Round to the nearest integer, as implied by the given test case (40.22... -> 40).\n    rounded_wind_chill = round(wind_chill_raw)\n    \n    return int(rounded_wind_chill)"}
