{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(array, position):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses elements in an array from index 0 up to a given position K (exclusive).\n    Returns a new array without modifying the original input array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n    \n    # Handle cases where position is out of bounds or zero\n    k = min(max(0, position), len(array))\n\n    # Slice the array into two parts: the part to be reversed and the rest\n    part_to_reverse = array[0:k]\n    remaining_part = array[k:]\n\n    # Reverse the first part\n    reversed_part = part_to_reverse[::-1]\n\n    # Concatenate the reversed part with the remaining part\n    return reversed_part + remaining_part"}
