{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(arr, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the rightmost insertion point for a target value in a sorted array.\n    Uses a binary search algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    left = 0\n    right = len(arr)\n\n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if arr[mid] <= target:  # If target is greater than or equal, we might need to go right\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:  # If target is less, we must go left\n            right = mid\n    return left"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/784", "solution": "def mul_even_odd(numbers):\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if first_even is None and num % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = num\n        if first_odd is None and num % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = num\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    if first_even is None or first_odd is None:\n        return 0\n    \n    return first_even * first_odd"}
